From: =?utf-8?b?T25kxZllaiBTdXLDvQ==?= <ondrej@sury.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:54:55 +0100
Subject: Lower the memory limit of the bug54268 test

The package is built with DTrace support, which makes every PHP function
call recurse on the C stack, so the endless recursion of this test
overflows the 8 MB stack before it reaches a memory limit of 8M (it does
up to 5M). Lower the limit to get to the error the test is about.
---
 Zend/tests/bug54268.phpt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Zend/tests/bug54268.phpt b/Zend/tests/bug54268.phpt
index b544cd8..a06112d 100644
--- a/Zend/tests/bug54268.phpt
+++ b/Zend/tests/bug54268.phpt
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 --TEST--
 Bug #54268 (Double free when destroy_zend_class fails)
 --INI--
-memory_limit=8M
+memory_limit=2M
 --SKIPIF--
 <?php
 $zend_mm_enabled = getenv("USE_ZEND_ALLOC");
